WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:15.421
The Leaning Tower of is one of the architectural wonders of the world, and permanently fascinating to people.

2
00:00:16.161 --> 00:00:19.203
The famous bell tower has stood for over six centuries.

3
00:00:20.604 --> 00:00:27.889
But it hasn't ever stood straight—at one point in history, the tower tilted about 4.5 meters from the

4
00:00:27.909 --> 00:00:32.072
vertical! Pisa is an ancient city in Tuscany, Italy.

5
00:00:32.804 --> 00:00:38.629
Located on the river Arno, with easy access to the sea, the city became a major port of

6
00:00:38.709 --> 00:00:46.174
trade. In the eleventh century, merchants from across the Mediterranean and as far away as the Middle East

7
00:00:46.594 --> 00:00:48.396
came to buy and sell goods.

8
00:00:50.017 --> 00:00:56.021
The city's inhabitants, the Pisans, often had to defend their city against outside forces.

9
00:00:57.242 --> 00:00:59.104
They also made their own conquests.

10
00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:05.424
In 1063 they sailed to the island of Sicily and attacked the city of Palermo.

11
00:01:06.785 --> 00:01:11.009
The defeat of Palermo made the Pisans rich and confident in their power.

12
00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:15.092
They decided to build a large cathedral to show off their treasures.

13
00:01:16.353 --> 00:01:21.056
A large piece of open land sat in the middle of the city, which the Pisans called the

14
00:01:21.156 --> 00:01:22.317
Square of Miracles.

15
00:01:23.238 --> 00:01:29.617
They decided to build the cathedral on the square, as a tribute to Pisa's conquests and rich heritage.

16
00:01:31.058 --> 00:01:35.239
The front of the building was covered with stones stolen from ancient Roman ruins.

17
00:01:37.019 --> 00:01:43.402
Even today you can read ancient Roman inscriptions, some of which are upside down or sideways, in the

18
00:01:43.442 --> 00:01:45.022
marble stones of the cathedral.

19
00:01:46.623 --> 00:01:50.884
The building took a very long time to complete, almost three hundred years.

20
00:01:52.832 --> 00:01:57.693
The Pisans also decided to build a cemetery and a tall bell tower in the square.

21
00:01:58.274 --> 00:02:04.055
Construction of the bell tower, which would later become known as the Leaning Tower of Pisa, began in

22
00:02:04.295 --> 00:02:11.837
1173. Not long after the workers had laid the foundation and built the first three floors, they noticed

23
00:02:11.857 --> 00:02:14.358
that the building was sinking on the south side.

24
00:02:15.559 --> 00:02:20.520
This was not surprising because the soil underneath the Square of Miracles was very marshy.

25
00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.243
It was a common problem for buildings in the area.

26
00:02:24.983 --> 00:02:29.027
In fact, the name Pisa means "marshy land" in Greek.

27
00:02:29.928 --> 00:02:35.273
Around this time war broke out, and construction on the bell tower stopped for nearly one hundred years.

28
00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:40.418
This long interruption turned out to be good for the tilting tower.

29
00:02:41.018 --> 00:02:47.104
It gave the building's foundation time to settle, and probably even prevented it from collapsing long ago.

30
00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:56.382
Experts believe that when construction on the tower restarted, an engineer named Bonanno Pisano was in charge of

31
00:02:56.422 --> 00:02:57.643
the challenging project.

32
00:02:58.483 --> 00:03:04.384
In order to compensate for the building's tilt, Pisano decided to make the columns and arches on the

33
00:03:04.444 --> 00:03:06.005
south side a little longer.

34
00:03:06.865 --> 00:03:08.826
He believed that this would level out the tower.

35
00:03:09.386 --> 00:03:12.266
But Pisano's solution only worsened the problem.

36
00:03:13.007 --> 00:03:15.747
The extra weight made the tower sink some more!

37
00:03:16.888 --> 00:03:22.955
As years passed, other engineers and builders took on the challenge of finishing the building, and fixing its

38
00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:29.379
tilt. By 1350 the tower's bell chamber had been constructed, and the rest of the tower was finally

39
00:03:29.479 --> 00:03:31.740
completed around 1372.

40
00:03:32.561 --> 00:03:38.144
When the tower was finished, many people were glad that all the builders had not quit the project.

41
00:03:38.744 --> 00:03:44.708
It was truly an architectural wonder, with beautiful arches and two hundred marble columns.

42
00:03:45.548 --> 00:03:48.329
But by now the tower's tilt was very noticeable.

43
00:03:48.789 --> 00:03:54.471
The tilt fascinated people, yet it worried them too; one day the tower could collapse.

44
00:03:55.091 --> 00:03:57.992
Over time many efforts were made to save the tower.

45
00:03:58.772 --> 00:04:03.313
Some of the solutions were realistic, while others were almost comical.

46
00:04:04.594 --> 00:04:10.915
One person suggested draining all of the water beneath the foundation of the tower; another suggested leaving the

47
00:04:10.955 --> 00:04:12.396
water there but freezing it!

48
00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:17.621
Other ideas included moving the tower to another location or rebuilding it.

49
00:04:18.141 --> 00:04:25.463
In the 1920s experts tried injecting cement into the foundation of the tower in order to stabilize it,

50
00:04:25.903 --> 00:04:28.364
or at least slow the rate at which it was tilting.

51
00:04:29.564 --> 00:04:33.665
Despite all these engineering efforts, the tower continued sinking.

52
00:04:34.406 --> 00:04:40.407
By the 1960s the Italian government was so concerned about the tower, they announced that they were looking

53
00:04:40.487 --> 00:04:43.328
for suggestions to solve this puzzling problem.

54
00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:49.307
Finally, in 1990, it was decided to close the building for safety reasons.

55
00:04:50.388 --> 00:04:53.970
A major project was eventually launched to straighten the tower.

56
00:04:54.930 --> 00:05:00.594
This time engineers slowly removed earth from underneath the foundation on its north side.

57
00:05:01.574 --> 00:05:07.218
When the tower reopened in 2001, the tilt had been reduced by about 44 centimeters!

58
00:05:07.998 --> 00:05:10.760
And over time the tilt decreased even more.

59
00:05:11.296 --> 00:05:16.499
The tall tower, with its unusual tilt, has fascinated not just builders and tourists.

60
00:05:17.299 --> 00:05:24.042
Galileo Galilei, a former resident of Pisa, was born about two hundred years after the tower was finished.

61
00:05:25.103 --> 00:05:28.724
He used it to conduct many important scientific experiments.

62
00:05:29.425 --> 00:05:35.828
In one famous story, Galileo wanted to prove his theory that all objects fall at the same speed.

63
00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:41.183
So he climbed to the top of the Tower of Pisa and dropped two balls at the same

64
00:05:41.263 --> 00:05:50.810
time. According to the story, both balls hit the ground at the same time even though they differed

65
00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.250
in weight.

66
00:05:52.531 --> 00:05:56.634
Today the bell tower continues to draw tourists and admirers from around the world.

67
00:05:58.415 --> 00:06:05.080
Engineers believe, due to recent measurements, that the building will remain stable now for at least two hundred

68
00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:12.506
years. So for generations to come, people can continue to look in amazement at the Leaning Tower of

69
00:06:12.607 --> 00:06:13.087
Pisa.
